{"id": "tea:dhyanabindu-upanisad:14", "source": "src:dhyanabindu-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "14"}, "paraphrase": "Oṃ is the bow, the self the arrow, Brahman the target; it is to be pierced by the heedful (quoting Muṇḍaka).", "tags": {"level": "bridging", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge", "meditation"], "stage": "intermediate"}, "types": ["sound-language", "practice"], "practices": ["prc:pranava-dhyana"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "sourced", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": [{"phase": "C", "date": "2026-09-29", "method": "text-locate", "queries": ["e-text dhyanabindu-upanisad 14"], "evidence": ["catalog:raw_etexts:108_Upanishads", "text:sources_raw/raw_etexts/vedaH/misc/upaniShat/mixedPF/108_Upanishads.md"], "result": "confirmed", "note": "E-text 14 located; the passage matches the paraphrase (it begins: 'oṃkāraṃ yo na jānāti brahmaṇo na bhavettu saḥ | praṇavodhanuḥ śaro hyātmā brahma tallekṣyamucyate || 14…').", "by": "sourcing:U04-minor-upanisads"}]}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:dhyanabindu-upanisad:19-21", "source": "src:dhyanabindu-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "19-21"}, "paraphrase": "Meditate on Oṃ as the thumb-sized Lord in the heart; Brahmā is inhalation, Viṣṇu retention, Rudra exhalation.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["meditation"], "stage": "intermediate"}, "types": ["practice", "sound-language"], "practices": ["prc:pranava-dhyana"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "sourced", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": [{"phase": "C", "date": "2026-09-29", "method": "text-locate", "queries": ["e-text dhyanabindu-upanisad 19-21"], "evidence": ["catalog:raw_etexts:108_Upanishads", "text:sources_raw/raw_etexts/vedaH/misc/upaniShat/mixedPF/108_Upanishads.md"], "result": "confirmed", "note": "E-text 19-21 located; the passage matches the paraphrase (it begins: 'hṛtpadmakarṇikā-madhye sthiradīpanibhākṛtim | aṅguṣṭhamātramacalaṃ dhyāyedaoṃkāramīśvaram || 19 ||iḍayā…').", "by": "sourcing:U04-minor-upanisads"}]}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:dhyanabindu-upanisad:41-43", "source": "src:dhyanabindu-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "41-43"}, "paraphrase": "Posture, breath-restraint, withdrawal, concentration, meditation and absorption are the six limbs. There are as many postures as beings; four are named — siddha, bhadra, siṃha and padma.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["body-breath"], "stage": "intermediate"}, "types": ["practice"], "paths": ["pth:dhyanabindu-six-limbs"], "practices": ["prc:asanas-yoga-upanisads"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "sourced", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": [{"phase": "C", "date": "2026-09-29", "method": "text-locate", "queries": ["e-text dhyanabindu-upanisad 41-43"], "evidence": ["catalog:raw_etexts:108_Upanishads", "text:sources_raw/raw_etexts/vedaH/misc/upaniShat/mixedPF/108_Upanishads.md"], "result": "confirmed", "note": "E-text 41-43 located; the passage matches the paraphrase (it begins: 'āsanamprāṇasaṃrodhaḥ pratyāhāraśca dhāraṇā | dhyānaṃ samādhiretāni yogāṅgāni bhavantiṣaṭ || 41 || āsanāni ca…').", "by": "sourcing:U04-minor-upanisads"}]}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:dhyanabindu-upanisad:43-54", "source": "src:dhyanabindu-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "43-54"}, "paraphrase": "The body's centres: the ādhāra with four petals and the triangle (yoni) and liṅga; the svādhiṣṭhāna; the maṇipūra, a twelve-spoked wheel where the jīva wanders driven by merit and sin; the kanda from which 72,000 channels spread, ten of them principal (iḍā, piṅgalā, suṣumnā, gāndhārī, hastijihvā, pūṣā, yaśasvinī, alambusā, kuhū, śaṅkhinī).", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "analytic", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["body-layers"], "concepts": ["cpt:cakras", "cpt:nadis"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "sourced", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": [{"phase": "C", "date": "2026-09-29", "method": "text-locate", "queries": ["e-text dhyanabindu-upanisad 43-54"], "evidence": ["catalog:raw_etexts:108_Upanishads", "text:sources_raw/raw_etexts/vedaH/misc/upaniShat/mixedPF/108_Upanishads.md"], "result": "confirmed", "note": "E-text 43-54 located; the passage matches the paraphrase (it begins: 'chidraṃ bhadraṃ tathā siṃhaṃ padmaṃ ceti catu-ṣṭayam | ādhāraṃ prathamaṃ cakraṃ svādhiṣṭhānaṃ dvitīyakam ||…').", "by": "sourcing:U04-minor-upanisads"}]}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:dhyanabindu-upanisad:58-60", "source": "src:dhyanabindu-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "58-60"}, "paraphrase": "The jīva, moved by prāṇa and apāna, goes up and down, never resting, like a ball struck by the hand, or a bird tied by a string that flies off and is pulled back.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "analytic", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["body-layers", "consciousness-mind"], "concepts": ["cpt:ten-vayus"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "sourced", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": [{"phase": "C", "date": "2026-09-29", "method": "text-locate", "queries": ["e-text dhyanabindu-upanisad 58-60"], "evidence": ["catalog:raw_etexts:108_Upanishads", "text:sources_raw/raw_etexts/vedaH/misc/upaniShat/mixedPF/108_Upanishads.md"], "result": "confirmed", "note": "E-text 58-60 located; the passage matches the paraphrase (it begins: 'ete nāḍīsahasreṣu vartante jīvarūpiṇaḥ |prāṇāpānavaśo jīvo hyadhaścordhvaṃ pradhāvati || 58 ||…').", "by": "sourcing:U04-minor-upanisads"}]}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:dhyanabindu-upanisad:61-65", "source": "src:dhyanabindu-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "61-65"}, "paraphrase": "The jīva goes out with the sound ha and returns with sa, repeating 'haṃsa' 21,600 times a day; this ajapā-gāyatrī gives liberation to yogins; knowing it one is freed from sin.", "tags": {"level": "bridging", "standpoint": "experiential", "naya": null, "path": ["sound", "meditation"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["sound-language", "practice"], "concepts": ["cpt:ajapa-gayatri", "cpt:hamsa"], "practices": ["prc:ajapa-japa"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "sourced", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": [{"phase": "C", "date": "2026-09-29", "method": "text-locate", "queries": ["e-text dhyanabindu-upanisad 61-65"], "evidence": ["catalog:raw_etexts:108_Upanishads", "text:sources_raw/raw_etexts/vedaH/misc/upaniShat/mixedPF/108_Upanishads.md"], "result": "confirmed", "note": "E-text 61-65 located; the passage matches the paraphrase (it begins: 'khagarajjuvadityetadyo jānāti sa yoga-vit | hakāreṇa bahiryāti sakāreṇa viśetpunaḥ || 61 || haṃsahaṃsetyamuṃ…').", "by": "sourcing:U04-minor-upanisads"}]}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:dhyanabindu-upanisad:66-68", "source": "src:dhyanabindu-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "66-68"}, "paraphrase": "The kuṇḍalinī sleeps covering with her mouth the door to Brahman; awakened by fire, mind and breath, she rises through the suṣumnā like a needle drawing thread; the yogin opens the door of liberation with her as a key opens a door.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "experiential", "naya": null, "path": ["body-breath", "meditation"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["body-layers", "powers-experiences"], "concepts": ["cpt:kundalini"], "practices": ["prc:sakticalana"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "sourced", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": [{"phase": "C", "date": "2026-09-29", "method": "text-locate", "queries": ["e-text dhyanabindu-upanisad 66-68"], "evidence": ["catalog:raw_etexts:108_Upanishads", "text:sources_raw/raw_etexts/vedaH/misc/upaniShat/mixedPF/108_Upanishads.md"], "result": "confirmed", "note": "E-text 66-68 located; the passage matches the paraphrase (it begins: 'mukhenā-cchādya taddvāraṃ prasuptā parameśvarī | prabuddhā vahniyogena manasā marutā saha|| 66 ||…').", "by": "sourcing:U04-minor-upanisads"}]}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:dhyanabindu-upanisad:79-92-summary", "source": "src:dhyanabindu-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "79-92 (summary)"}, "paraphrase": "Khecarī mudrā and the retention of bindu are described: bindu is twofold, white (śukla, Śiva) and red (rajas, Śakti), and their union in the body is the yogin's aim. Recorded as a summary only.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["body-breath"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["practice", "body-layers"], "practices": ["prc:khecari-mudra"], "concepts": ["cpt:bindu"], "restricted": true, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "sourced", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": [{"phase": "C", "date": "2026-09-29", "method": "text-locate", "queries": ["e-text dhyanabindu-upanisad 79-92 (summary)"], "evidence": ["catalog:raw_etexts:108_Upanishads", "text:sources_raw/raw_etexts/vedaH/misc/upaniShat/mixedPF/108_Upanishads.md"], "result": "confirmed", "note": "E-text 79-92 (summary) located; the passage matches the paraphrase (it begins: 'na pīyūṣaṃ patatyagnau na ca vāyuḥ pradhāvati | kapālakuhare jihvāpraviṣṭā viparītagā || 79 ||…').", "by": "sourcing:U04-minor-upanisads"}]}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:dhyanabindu-upanisad:9-12", "source": "src:dhyanabindu-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "9-12"}, "paraphrase": "Oṃ's letters correspond to Vedas, worlds and deities; a is yellow and of rajas, u white and of sattva, m black and of tamas.", "tags": {"level": "bridging", "standpoint": "experiential", "naya": null, "path": ["sound", "meditation"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["sound-language"], "concepts": ["cpt:omkara-matras"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "sourced", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": [{"phase": "C", "date": "2026-09-29", "method": "text-locate", "queries": ["e-text dhyanabindu-upanisad 9-12"], "evidence": ["catalog:raw_etexts:108_Upanishads", "text:sources_raw/raw_etexts/vedaH/misc/upaniShat/mixedPF/108_Upanishads.md"], "result": "confirmed", "note": "E-text 9-12 located; the passage matches the paraphrase (it begins: 'omityekākṣaraṃ brahma dhyeyaṃ sarvamumukṣubhiḥ | pṛthivyagniścaṛgvedo bhūrityeva pitāmahaḥ || 9 || akāre tu…').", "by": "sourcing:U04-minor-upanisads"}]}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:dhyanabindu-upanisad:93-94-petal-moods", "source": "src:dhyanabindu-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "93-94 (petal moods)"}, "paraphrase": "In the heart lotus the moods follow the petals: east (white) dharma, south-east (red) sleep and sloth, south (black) hatred, south-west (blue) sin and violence, west (crystal) play, north-west (ruby) going and dispassion, north (yellow) pleasure, north-east (lapis) charity; at the junctions, disease; at the centre, knowing all.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "experiential", "naya": null, "path": ["body-breath", "meditation"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["consciousness-mind"], "concepts": ["cpt:heart-lotus-petals"], "cross_refs": ["tea:hamsa-upanisad:3-heart-lotus"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "sourced", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": [{"phase": "C", "date": "2026-09-29", "method": "text-locate", "queries": ["e-text dhyanabindu-upanisad 93-94 (petal moods)"], "evidence": ["catalog:raw_etexts:108_Upanishads", "text:sources_raw/raw_etexts/vedaH/misc/upaniShat/mixedPF/108_Upanishads.md"], "result": "confirmed", "note": "E-text 93-94 (petal moods) located; the passage matches the paraphrase (it begins: 'vakṣonyastahanurni-pīḍya suṣiraṃ yoneśca vāmāṅghriṇā hastābhyāmanudhārayanpravitataṃ pādaṃ tathādakṣiṇam |…').", "by": "sourcing:U04-minor-upanisads"}]}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:dhyanabindu-upanisad:94-five-states", "source": "src:dhyanabindu-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "94 (five states)"}, "paraphrase": "Resting in the successive circles of the lotus the self experiences waking, dream, deep sleep, the fourth and what is beyond the fourth.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "experiential", "naya": null, "path": ["body-breath", "meditation"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["consciousness-mind"], "concepts": ["cpt:turiya-turiyatita"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "sourced", "confidence": "low", "unverified": false, "checks": [{"phase": "C", "date": "2026-09-29", "method": "text-locate", "queries": ["e-text dhyanabindu-upanisad 94 (five states)"], "evidence": ["catalog:raw_etexts:108_Upanishads", "text:sources_raw/raw_etexts/vedaH/misc/upaniShat/mixedPF/108_Upanishads.md"], "result": "confirmed", "note": "E-text 94 (five states) located; the passage matches the paraphrase (it begins: 'athātmanirṇayaṃ vyākhyāsye || hṛdi-sthāne aṣṭadalapadmaṃ vartate tanmadhye rekhāvalayaṃ kṛtvā jīvātmarūpaṃ…').", "by": "sourcing:U04-minor-upanisads"}]}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
